# Files preserved across `sysupgrade`. Same format as /etc/sysupgrade.conf
# — one path per line. OpenWrt's sysupgrade walks /lib/upgrade/keep.d/*
# and adds every line to the backup tar before writing the new image,
# then restores from the tar after first boot.
#
# What's in /etc/rasputin/:
#   - seed.env         operator-supplied controlplane URL + join token
#                      (delivered by the controlplane's bootstrap_firewall
#                      job or hand-edited; MUST survive sysupgrade or
#                      every firmware update would reset the firewall
#                      back to unconfigured state).
#   - trust/root-ca.pem  CI-injected at build, but if the operator ever
#                      rotates it locally that change should survive too.
#
# /etc/config/rasputin (UCI) is deliberately NOT in this list — it's
# regenerated by /usr/lib/rasputin/apply-seed on every boot from
# seed.env. Preserving it would just mask seed.env changes.
#
# Discovered during the CWWK x86-p5-n100 sysupgrade test 2026-06-07.
/etc/rasputin/
